<description>
Dock movable tools into border-anchored frames by filling cavities.

Input structure:
- bg = most common color.
- Border-touching components cluster into anchor frames with interior bg cavities.
- Non-border 2-color components are movable tools.

Rule:
- Match each tool to a frame whose cavity size equals one of its color-region counts.
- Rotate/flip the tool so one color fills the cavity exactly; the other stays outside.
- If the docking orientation uses a reflection, swap the tool's two colors.

Key insight: Cavity size determines tool–frame pairing; reflection triggers color swap.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "move_to_match",
  "src": "sprite s not touching the edges",
  "dst": "dock into frames d on edge",
  "match_cond": "s.component.shape == d.notch.shape with rotation/flip",
  "transform": "swap colors of the two components of s if flip is used"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 18-30 rows x 25-30 cols
  bg: most common color
  num_pairs: 1-2 frame-tool pairs
  frame:
    structure: 2 same-color 4-connected sub-components, both touching the SAME single border (top/bottom/left/right)
    sub_components: separated by exactly 1 empty row or col (perpendicular to border)
    one_sub: full rectangle (bar), the other has a staircase notch at one corner
    notch: 1-3 cells, always a staircase (upper-triangular) shape
    combined_bbox: 3-7 rows x 4-7 cols
    cavity: bg region inside combined bbox adjacent to frame; size 5-8 cells
    cavity_shape: staircase shape (formed by gap row/col + notch)
    frame_color: single color, distinct from bg; two frames may share a color
  tool:
    structure: single 4-connected component NOT touching any border; exactly 2 colors (plug + handle)
    each_color_region: 4-connected, 4-9 pixels each
    plug_count: equals exactly one frame's cavity size (determines pairing)
    plug_shape: matches cavity shape under some rotation/flip from the D4 group
    handle: adjacent to plug, extends in the direction away from the frame's border
    total_size: 10-15 pixels
    inter_color_boundary: 1-2 shared edges between plug and handle regions
    separation: tool placed far from its target frame (>=4 Manhattan distance)
  transform:
    plug_color fills cavity exactly; handle protrudes outward from frame
    if docking uses a reflection (flip) AND plug/handle have unequal counts, swap the two tool colors
    tool is removed from original position; output = frame + docked tool only

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first
  steps:
    1. Pick grid size, bg color, and number of pairs (1-2).
    2. For each pair, build the DOCKED output state first:
       a. Choose a border side and position; build the frame (2 sub-comps of one color with 1-row/col gap and staircase notch) creating a cavity of size C.
       b. Generate a 2-color tool where plug region has exactly C pixels matching cavity shape, handle region has H pixels (H != C preferred) and is 4-connected to plug, extending away from the border.
       c. Place the docked tool so plug fills cavity exactly, handle protrudes outward.
    3. Verify the assembled output is valid (no overlaps, all components touch border).
    4. Derive input by UNDOING the docking: pick a random rotation/flip for the tool (possibly different from docking transform), if flip status changes and counts are unequal then swap colors back, place tool at a distant bg-only location on the grid.
    5. Erase the tool from its docked position (restore bg), keeping only the frame.
```
</generation_spec>
